# Copy to .env and edit. Nothing here is secret; it is machine layout.

# Where you unzipped the ATAK CIV SDK. It must be the folder that directly
# contains atak.apk, android_keystore and atak-gradle-takdev.jar.
# Download it yourself from https://tak.gov — it is licensed material and is
# deliberately not baked into the image or committed to any repository.
ATAK_SDK_DIR=/home/you/development/tak/ATAK-CIV-5.8.0.1-SDK

# The directory holding your plugin repositories, mounted at /work. Point it
# at the parent folder, not at one plugin: several agents can then work on
# different plugins, or different git worktrees of one plugin, at the same
# time without sharing a checkout.
#
#   /work/atak-plugin-alpha
#   /work/atak-plugin-beta
#   /work/atak-plugin-alpha.worktrees/some-branch
PLUGINS_DIR=/home/you/development/tak

# Your host's adb key directory, so the emulator does not re-prompt to
# authorise the container. Defaults to $HOME/.android.
#ANDROID_USER_HOME=/home/you/.android

# How the container reaches the host's adb server. The default works on
# WSL2 / Docker Desktop. On native Linux Docker try 127.0.0.1:5037.
#ADB_BRIDGE_TARGET=host.docker.internal:5037

# Optional. Passed through so an agent inside the container can use `gh`
# without a separate login.
#GH_TOKEN=ghp_...
